WEBVTT

00:16.470 --> 00:17.430
That person...

00:18.640 --> 00:19.640
She's crying?

00:23.620 --> 00:24.570
Are you okay?

00:51.150 --> 00:57.870
Shining stars away bless

00:58.200 --> 01:03.080
chiisakutonaeru mahou no kotobawa

00:58.200 --> 01:03.080
Silently chanting the magical words

01:03.960 --> 01:05.710
『onegai。。。』

01:03.960 --> 01:05.710
"please"

01:06.000 --> 01:11.340
hoshizora samayou kaze ni notta maigo notsubu

01:06.000 --> 01:11.340
The lost grain riding the wind on the sky

01:11.340 --> 01:12.380
『kizuite。。。』

01:11.340 --> 01:12.380
Please notice

01:12.380 --> 01:20.260
tsutawara nakute porori ochita kono omoi

01:12.380 --> 01:20.260
Untold words, teardrops of feelings that fell down

01:20.760 --> 01:27.350
kagayaki dasuyo GARASU bin nonaka

01:20.760 --> 01:27.350
Show your shine inside the glass bottle

01:27.730 --> 01:34.740
manten no hoshi deatta KISEKI kimi ga soba ni itekureru nara

01:27.730 --> 01:34.740
If you will stay beside me perfect star of encountered miracles...

01:34.900 --> 01:42.120
Whatever the mystery, I will be able to gather my courage.

01:35.320 --> 01:42.120
donna fushigi mouke tomeru yuuki umare te yuku yo

01:42.450 --> 01:49.710
nanatsuiro ni hikaru houseki sora kara mai oriru

01:42.450 --> 01:49.710
Seven colored glittering gems flying down from the sky

01:49.710 --> 01:53.420
Scoop up the important fragments

01:50.130 --> 01:53.420
daijina KAKERA sukui agerune

01:53.420 --> 01:58.930
kowasa nuyou sotto。。。

01:53.420 --> 01:58.930
And secretly hold onto them tight

02:06.070 --> 02:08.870
Summer break ends too quickly.

02:08.870 --> 02:12.320
What should I do? I haven't even finished my homework yet.

02:12.320 --> 02:13.850
Me neither.

02:22.270 --> 02:24.320
There is someone, right? Someone you like.

02:25.690 --> 02:30.780
<i>The one Akihime likes... is Kisaragi-sensei?</i>

02:37.220 --> 02:40.070
For what reason... am I hiding?

02:40.960 --> 02:43.320
Good morning, Tsuwabuki-sama.

02:46.680 --> 02:48.420
Oh, hello.

02:48.420 --> 02:51.310
Oh, right. May I have a bit of your time?

02:51.670 --> 02:52.620
Yes?

02:54.360 --> 02:58.350
The Warm Light of Evening

03:00.870 --> 03:01.940
Miss.

03:02.970 --> 03:04.820
I have brought Tsuwabuki-sama.

03:06.320 --> 03:07.820
Matsuda, you may go now.

03:08.020 --> 03:09.530
Yes, Miss.

03:14.270 --> 03:15.840
Umm, what?

03:17.520 --> 03:20.470
About that incident... You didn't tell anyone, right?

03:20.470 --> 03:22.120
Eh? What incident?

03:23.710 --> 03:25.170
The incident at camp!

03:25.320 --> 03:28.520
At camp? Oh, you mean when I carried you during the courage...

03:28.520 --> 03:29.480
Not so loud!

03:35.050 --> 03:38.020
I won't tell anyone, I promise.

03:38.620 --> 03:41.140
And this conversation too. Don't tell anyone.

03:41.930 --> 03:43.810
Matsuda, let's go.

03:43.810 --> 03:45.230
Yes, Miss.

03:47.770 --> 03:48.770
Excuse us.

04:16.270 --> 04:20.170
<i>No matter who Akihime likes, it's none of my business.</i>

04:23.730 --> 04:26.440
<i>Though that's what I thought...  </i>

04:27.970 --> 04:29.070
<i>Then why...</i>

04:49.470 --> 04:51.630
Sumomo, don't push yourself too much.

04:51.630 --> 04:54.230
It's good to rest when you need to.

04:58.120 --> 04:59.640
Nako-chan...

05:00.220 --> 05:01.370
What happened?

05:04.020 --> 05:05.360
Yaeno-san.

05:06.120 --> 05:11.220
Sorry, the shop wasn't open today and I came to help, but...

05:12.320 --> 05:13.690
Did something happen?

05:16.670 --> 05:19.720
N-Nothing's wrong. But thank you.

05:24.770 --> 05:25.670
Haru!

05:28.960 --> 05:31.250
There was nothing to do, so...

05:31.250 --> 05:34.960
While bringing food I came to help on something.

05:41.720 --> 05:44.320
You know that you can eat sunflower seeds, right?

05:44.320 --> 05:49.370
Since it should taste better than the ones we sell, I thought of trying one.

05:49.580 --> 05:52.620
Eh? Was it okay?

05:52.620 --> 05:57.110
Actually, it tasted horrible. It was really bitter.

05:58.970 --> 06:01.570
Noboku-san told me this:

06:01.570 --> 06:03.320
"That T-shirt doesn't suit you."

06:03.320 --> 06:06.520
"If it were summer, it would suit you better."

06:06.520 --> 06:08.000
So I said this:

06:08.000 --> 06:12.220
It's okay for someone who is weak and without muscles to wear it in summer, right?

06:12.220 --> 06:14.420
Akihime-san, what do you think?

06:21.670 --> 06:24.720
<i>If I could talk like that, I would… </i>

06:25.170 --> 06:27.820
Tsuwabuki, that's not a weed.

06:27.820 --> 06:29.720
Eh? Ah, sorry.

06:31.690 --> 06:33.810
I... think I should go home for today.

06:45.220 --> 06:48.020
Right! When I'm Yuki-chan, I can talk more about certain things.

06:51.420 --> 06:53.520
I’m so pitiful...

07:00.020 --> 07:01.840
Welcome, Yuki-chan.

07:03.170 --> 07:04.720
This is... an acorn?

07:05.600 --> 07:08.350
It was on the ground at the greenhouse.

07:08.350 --> 07:11.070
It was all alone stuck on the ground, so...

07:11.970 --> 07:14.730
It looked like a stray.

07:14.730 --> 07:18.360
A stray? Sumomo thinks of interesting things.

07:18.770 --> 07:21.450
Normally, looking at an acorn you wouldn't think of it like that.

07:23.860 --> 07:26.410
Sumomo, did something happen?

07:27.090 --> 07:33.620
Ore, err... I'll listen to you if there's anything you want to tell me. You might even feel refreshed after doing so.

07:34.570 --> 07:37.520
Thank you Yuki-chan, you're so kind.

07:37.970 --> 07:40.460
When I saw this, I remembered...

07:40.820 --> 07:44.390
During the entrance ceremony a year ago in spring...

07:46.120 --> 07:49.640
In the cherry blossom forest behind the school,

07:49.640 --> 07:52.230
I got lost.

07:53.320 --> 07:55.770
I had gotten separated from Nako-chan.

07:59.320 --> 08:02.520
<i>You had gotten lost during... the entrance ceremony?</i>

08:07.120 --> 08:08.240
<i>Could it be...? </i>

08:09.320 --> 08:13.500
I... was nervous and scared.

08:13.500 --> 08:15.520
I was about to cry.

08:16.380 --> 08:17.710
But then...

08:23.340 --> 08:25.270
I met this boy...

08:26.720 --> 08:29.640
<i>The girl from back then was... Sumomo?  </i>

08:30.470 --> 08:37.060
He was also a new student, and he even took me all the way back to the entrance ceremony.

08:37.420 --> 08:40.950
I was… very happy.

08:41.170 --> 08:44.450
Sumomo, about that person, do you...

08:45.990 --> 08:46.960
Yes.

08:49.320 --> 08:52.720
But, it may be that my first love won't come true.

08:54.010 --> 08:57.330
Because that person already has someone that they like...

08:58.370 --> 08:59.220
Sumomo!

09:01.670 --> 09:02.820
The ring!

09:11.420 --> 09:12.400
What?!

09:14.850 --> 09:18.940
This place was a waterway for children. Earlier...

09:19.620 --> 09:22.400
Because the star drop went in, it became like this?

09:24.820 --> 09:26.220
The star drop!

09:26.620 --> 09:28.280
Sumomo, are you okay?

09:28.990 --> 09:30.120
I'll give it a try...

09:35.170 --> 09:36.540
Ruche Puria...

09:38.120 --> 09:40.590
Still weak against water, I see.

09:43.710 --> 09:46.440
And you still call yourself a Stellar Spinear?

09:46.620 --> 09:47.870
Aspalas-san?

09:48.050 --> 09:50.470
Prima Aspalas!

09:50.470 --> 09:52.670
Say it right!

09:53.350 --> 09:57.450
Whatever. In order to see who the superior Stellar Spinear is, this a battle.

09:57.450 --> 10:00.160
But… A battle?

10:00.420 --> 10:01.820
Enough talk!

10:03.420 --> 10:05.320
Beam Cometi Aqua!

10:11.820 --> 10:13.370
Ara Deum Mei!

10:17.620 --> 10:18.580
Sumomo?

10:18.720 --> 10:21.580
I'll try my very best!

10:21.720 --> 10:22.960
Sumomo?

10:23.020 --> 10:24.920
Beam Cometi Aqua!

10:48.470 --> 10:49.700
Somehow you made it.

10:49.870 --> 10:52.320
It’s a full on fair and square battle!

11:01.920 --> 11:04.960
Sumomo! Sumomo!!!

11:17.320 --> 11:18.020
Sumomo!

11:23.720 --> 11:24.470
Got it!

11:26.820 --> 11:27.320
It's fast!

11:27.920 --> 11:31.000
Miss please be careful, that star drop is no push over.

11:32.120 --> 11:33.320
Just as I expected.

11:33.320 --> 11:36.080
It should be this difficult for it to be worthwhile.

11:36.520 --> 11:38.170
Sumomo, are you okay?

11:38.620 --> 11:41.880
If I make a mistake, I quickly cry.

11:42.570 --> 11:45.620
But Yuki-chan is with me so I’ll try my best.

11:46.760 --> 11:49.120
Sumomo, it’s a new Recipe!

11:53.020 --> 11:55.890
Moterios Oludin Radium!

12:11.770 --> 12:12.440
Miss!

12:32.170 --> 12:34.350
Puruvi Radius!

12:41.440 --> 12:45.700
Spectacular! Miss is the complete victor!

12:45.700 --> 12:46.980
Uh, Miss?

12:46.980 --> 12:49.370
<i>What was that… that previous technique?</i>

12:49.820 --> 12:52.870
<i>The Recipe that even I, the best in Saint Aspalas, don’t know… </i>

12:53.670 --> 12:55.120
<i>How can this girl… </i>

12:58.420 --> 13:01.950
P-Please wait Miss! Miss!

13:04.520 --> 13:06.800
Sumomo! Sumomo, are you okay?

13:06.920 --> 13:08.520
Yuki-chan, I’m sorry.

13:09.770 --> 13:12.930
After all that, the star drop... I lost it.

13:13.170 --> 13:15.920
E-Everybody fails from time to time.

13:15.920 --> 13:17.570
You just need to try harder again next time.

13:19.320 --> 13:22.050
I can’t even keep the promise I made with Yuki-chan.

13:23.820 --> 13:24.870
I’m sorry.

13:25.770 --> 13:27.320
Sumomo...

13:36.070 --> 13:38.950
And so, Akihime is really depressed...

13:40.720 --> 13:44.920
Undoubtedly, losing the battle last night was disheartening.

13:45.270 --> 13:46.670
You don’t get it, do you?

13:49.420 --> 13:52.670
Listen carefully. The power of a Stellar Spinear's spell...

13:52.670 --> 13:57.720
The magic’s power reflects the power of the user’s heart.

13:59.420 --> 14:00.120
Their heart?

14:00.920 --> 14:05.320
If something good happens and her heart is happy, then her power increases.

14:05.620 --> 14:10.670
On the other hand, if something sad happens or depression sets in, their power begins to decrease.

14:11.670 --> 14:12.770
Something sad?

14:13.570 --> 14:17.520
Tsuwabuki-kun, is there anything you know?

14:19.720 --> 14:20.520
Who knows…

14:20.970 --> 14:24.080
You don’t know, even though you guys are always together?

14:24.080 --> 14:26.870
E-Even if you say that…

14:27.970 --> 14:33.720
In these situations, I believe that girls will cheer up if they get attention from the person they like.

14:41.610 --> 14:45.220
He took me all the way back to the entrance ceremony.

14:45.220 --> 14:47.110
I was… very happy.

14:47.370 --> 14:51.060
Even if... Akihime really likes me...

14:51.060 --> 14:55.570
As of right now, I can't do anything for her.

14:56.770 --> 14:59.120
It’ll always be troublesome for Akihime.

14:59.700 --> 15:01.740
I can't say anything about what I heard yesterday.

15:02.070 --> 15:04.570
And even more so to smile.

15:06.670 --> 15:07.290
Here.

15:08.240 --> 15:09.660
Have some.

15:09.660 --> 15:11.870
I got the yakisoba bread.

15:11.870 --> 15:12.830
No thanks.

15:12.830 --> 15:14.820
Why? It’s your favorite.

15:15.820 --> 15:17.420
I don’t have any appetite.

15:20.270 --> 15:24.890
Maybe Tsuwabuki-kun is in love or something.

15:25.670 --> 15:27.820
In love?! W-What?!

15:32.920 --> 15:35.200
I'm right, am I not?

15:36.270 --> 15:38.610
Seriously?! Haru in love?

15:38.610 --> 15:40.400
Lies! It can't be!

15:42.170 --> 15:44.540
I mean, it's possible, yes.

15:44.540 --> 15:46.920
But... I'm not really sure...

15:47.540 --> 15:49.320
It may be that staying as friends is what she wants.

15:53.070 --> 15:55.210
That girl, what's she like?

15:55.390 --> 15:56.770
What she's like...

15:59.820 --> 16:01.920
She cries easily.

16:02.560 --> 16:05.270
She's small and insecure.

16:05.770 --> 16:08.650
But, she always tries her best.

16:09.650 --> 16:14.110
She tries hard, and she's very kind-hearted.

16:15.190 --> 16:17.990
I can believe that. There's no mistake about it.

16:18.170 --> 16:19.480
So it's something like this, right?

16:19.480 --> 16:24.530
Tsuwabuki-kun is thinking, "I cannot do anything for that girl," or...

16:24.530 --> 16:26.780
"Even if I confess it would only cause trouble."

16:26.780 --> 16:28.870
Something like that, right?

16:31.800 --> 16:33.070
But you know, Haru...

16:34.470 --> 16:38.220
Those things aren't important to girls.

16:40.270 --> 16:42.830
Keisuke-kun, did something happen with Nobuko?

16:43.850 --> 16:46.940
W-Well, this really isn't about Nobuko-san.

16:48.220 --> 16:49.720
But, as he said...

16:50.770 --> 16:53.450
The important thing is to be honest with your feelings, right?

17:00.220 --> 17:01.900
A confession!

17:01.900 --> 17:04.360
Right! I should tag along and...

17:04.360 --> 17:06.210
Let's just observe quietly.

17:06.200 --> 17:09.880
No, no. I'm worried about Haru confessing properly.

17:09.880 --> 17:13.670
I’m telling you not to interfere. Got it?

17:14.720 --> 17:15.630
Y-Yes…

17:20.620 --> 17:23.320
I have no confidence even though I'm running fast.

17:25.270 --> 17:27.670
But...  But...

17:31.070 --> 17:32.340
Even so...

17:35.130 --> 17:35.920
I...

17:59.890 --> 18:00.720
Aki-

18:03.360 --> 18:06.820
<i>If I...  If I don’t say anything... </i>

18:08.740 --> 18:10.310
But, what...?

18:11.590 --> 18:13.890
Tsuwabuki-kun, what’s wrong?

18:14.920 --> 18:15.680
Well, I...

18:16.320 --> 18:20.520
That is... I was thinking about that flower I was arranging.

18:20.740 --> 18:22.360
Me too.

18:22.360 --> 18:26.920
I couldn't take care of this place a lot.

18:29.670 --> 18:31.920
I wanted to do something for it.

18:35.720 --> 18:36.720
I’ll help.

18:55.920 --> 18:58.420
Not good. It’s almost time.

18:59.810 --> 19:04.420
T-Tsuwabuki-kun... Umm, come this way...

19:05.920 --> 19:09.830
Could you please come with me?

19:37.420 --> 19:39.620
Try standing here.

19:40.420 --> 19:42.370
Akihime, what…

20:03.470 --> 20:04.520
This is…

20:08.070 --> 20:09.520
During the sunset...

20:10.470 --> 20:12.870
For a short while...

20:14.620 --> 20:17.070
It shines likes this.

20:20.290 --> 20:21.670
Amazing.

20:23.190 --> 20:25.870
It’s very beautiful.

20:35.420 --> 20:37.910
U-Umm...

20:37.910 --> 20:42.820
Can we keep this as a secret, just between you and me?

20:42.820 --> 20:46.750
Only us? Does Yaeno not know?

20:47.130 --> 20:47.840
That's right.

20:48.380 --> 20:53.300
I kept it a secret from everyone, even Nako.

20:54.220 --> 20:58.920
For me, when I’m depressed I come here and watch this.

20:59.570 --> 21:02.270
It cheers me up a little.

21:03.320 --> 21:08.980
Tsuwabuki-kun, you looked like you didn’t have any energy.

21:08.980 --> 21:14.960
So I thought that if you saw this, you might cheer up a bit.

21:18.070 --> 21:19.370
<i>Akihime. </i>

21:20.000 --> 21:23.320
<i>Even though you went through all that… </i>

21:25.420 --> 21:28.460
For me... you...

21:39.320 --> 21:40.420
Akihime.

21:42.720 --> 21:43.720
I’m sorry.

21:44.870 --> 21:46.170
The reason why I came here...

21:47.600 --> 21:50.980
And how worried I was about the flowers was a lie.

21:51.720 --> 21:53.290
R-Really?

21:54.620 --> 22:00.120
I was actually looking for you... Akihime.

22:03.140 --> 22:03.990
I...

22:09.920 --> 22:14.770
I… like you, Akihime.

22:51.540 --> 22:55.090
kira kira no hoshikuzu ha maru de

22:51.540 --> 22:55.090
Fragments of glittering stars

22:55.090 --> 22:58.380
koi suru otome no kiseki

22:55.090 --> 22:58.380
are just like the miracles of a girl in love

22:58.630 --> 23:02.180
kinou mada no watashi ha doko he

22:58.630 --> 23:02.180
Where did the cleverness from yesterday go,

23:02.180 --> 23:05.100
nanika chigau RABIRINSU

23:02.180 --> 23:05.100
Since it's like a labyrinth now

23:05.600 --> 23:09.350
dan dan wakan naku naru

23:05.600 --> 23:09.350
Slowly becoming confused

23:09.520 --> 23:12.360
（doushi you　doushi you）

23:09.520 --> 23:12.360
What do I do? What do I do?

23:12.610 --> 23:19.570
don don afurete kuru　AH　HAHAHA

23:12.610 --> 23:19.570
Slowly becoming overflowed

23:19.740 --> 23:25.450
yume no naka jya　nandemo ieru no ni…

23:19.740 --> 23:25.450
But inside a dream, can't you say anything?

23:25.450 --> 23:29.080
yuuki kudasai

23:25.450 --> 23:29.080
Please give me courage

23:30.370 --> 23:32.000
mo-o！

23:30.370 --> 23:32.000
Mo-o!

23:32.170 --> 23:36.840
konna ni aitai no ni

23:32.170 --> 23:36.840
I really want to meet you

23:36.840 --> 23:39.130
kanari Bi-myo

23:36.840 --> 23:39.130
Proxy doll

23:39.300 --> 23:43.050
toki meki ga koi no saidai no teki

23:39.300 --> 23:43.050
This throbbing is love's biggest challenge

23:43.050 --> 23:44.640
jirettai no yo

23:43.050 --> 23:44.640
It's irritating

23:44.640 --> 23:45.970
ne-e

23:44.640 --> 23:45.970
Isn't it?

23:46.390 --> 23:51.100
yume kara sametara mata

23:46.390 --> 23:51.100
The reasons to wake again

23:51.100 --> 23:56.650
kobore souna kimi no egao ni

23:51.100 --> 23:56.650
Are overflowing to see your smile

23:56.650 --> 23:59.570
airu kana

23:56.650 --> 23:59.570
If we meet again

24:10.220 --> 24:13.270
Sumomo-chan’s father is a well-known author.

24:13.270 --> 24:14.020
And her mother?

24:14.020 --> 24:15.570
That is a mystery.

24:15.570 --> 24:16.720
She's in another country right?

24:16.720 --> 24:17.320
I see.

24:17.320 --> 24:19.180
Rumor has it that she's very beautiful.

24:19.180 --> 24:20.750
Just like a goddess.

24:20.750 --> 24:22.820
I want a date with her.

24:21.980 --> 24:24.900
Episode 7

24:21.980 --> 24:24.900
Honey Colored Hesitation

24:22.820 --> 24:24.390
Think of the age difference!
